        261.980224609375,
        303.7789306640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This section reviews related algorithms for legged robot lo-",
      "bbox": [
        63.96299743652344,
        309.7953796386719,
        298.8013610839844,
        318.7019348144531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "comotion and manipulation and relevant literature on MPPI.",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        321.7503662109375,
        298.8010559082031,
        330.65692138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A. Locomotion and Manipulation for Legged Robots",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        339.4990234375,
        269.8197021484375,
        348.0867919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Current algorithms for legged robot locomotion and ma-",
      "bbox": [
        63.96299743652344,
        354.3323669433594,
        298.80133056640625,
        363.2389221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "nipulation generally fall into two categories: gradient-based",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        366.287353515625,
        298.8009948730469,
        375.19390869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model-predictive control (MPC) [8]–[11] and gradient-free",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        378.2423400878906,
        298.8009033203125,
        387.1488952636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reinforcement learning (RL) [12]–[15]. MPC policies lever-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        390.19732666015625,
        298.8009033203125,
        399.1038818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "age first or second-order gradient information from the",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        402.1523132324219,
        298.80096435546875,
        411.0588684082031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model to achieve real-time policy optimization without any",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        414.1083068847656,
        298.8009948730469,
        423.0148620605469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "offline computation. Despite the obvious pitfalls of relying",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        426.06329345703125,
        298.80096435546875,
        434.9698486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on simplified models, MPC has been a staple for real-world",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        438.0182800292969,
        298.8009948730469,
        446.9248352050781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "deployment of legged robots and demonstrates impressive",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        449.9732666015625,
        298.8009948730469,
        458.87982177734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generalization to different robots and surprising robustness to",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        461.9282531738281,
        298.8009948730469,
        470.8348083496094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model mismatch, even on challenging terrains. However, due",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        473.8842468261719,
        298.8009948730469,
        482.7908020019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to real-time and onboard computation requirements for these",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        485.8392333984375,
        298.8009338378906,
        494.74578857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithms, simplified models are often employed and only",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        497.7942199707031,
        298.8009948730469,
        506.7007751464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "contacts between the feet and the terrain are considered [11],",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        509.74920654296875,
        298.801025390625,
        518.65576171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[16], preventing these model-based policies from taking",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        521.7042236328125,
        298.801025390625,
        530.6107788085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "full advantage of the robot’s dynamics and leveraging full-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        533.6591796875,
        298.8009033203125,
        542.5657348632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "body contact to solve complicated locomotion or manip-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        545.6151733398438,
        298.8009338378906,
        554.521728515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ulation tasks. Existing approaches for model-based loco-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        557.5701904296875,
        298.80096435546875,
        566.4767456054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "manipulation require introducing manually designed task-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        569.5252075195312,
        298.80096435546875,
        578.4317626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "specific contact pairs to the model [17], [18], significantly",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        581.480224609375,
        298.8009338378906,
        590.3867797851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "limiting generalization capabilities when facing new tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        593.4351806640625,
        293.441162109375,
        602.3417358398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the other hand, simulation-based RL has shown im-",
      "bbox": [
        63.96299743652344,
        605.22021484375,
        298.8013916015625,
        614.1267700195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pressive progress in recent years thanks to improved sim-to-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        617.1751708984375,
        298.80096435546875,
        626.0817260742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "real transfer via domain randomization techniques [12], [14]",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        629.1312255859375,
        298.8009033203125,
        638.0377807617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and efficient parallel simulation on modern hardware [19]–",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        641.086181640625,
        298.80096435546875,
        649.9927368164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[21]. The fundamental difference between simulation-based",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        653.0411987304688,
        298.8009948730469,
        661.94775390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RL and MPC is that RL attempts to learn a neural network",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        664.9962158203125,
        298.801025390625,
        673.9027709960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "policy offline through large-scale trial-and-error in simula-",
      "bbox": [
        53.999996185302734,
        676.951171875,
        298.8009338378906,
        685.8577270507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion. In this offline policy optimization regime without real-",
      "bbox": [
        53.99999237060547,
        688.9061889648438,
        298.8009033203125,
        697.812744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "time computation constraints, it is standard to train policies",
      "bbox": [
        53.99999237060547,
        700.8621826171875,
        298.8009948730469,
        709.7687377929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by simulating whole-body robot dynamics and collision",
      "bbox": [
        53.99999237060547,
        712.8171997070312,
        298.8009033203125,
        721.7237548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "geometries from all parts of the robot and its environment,",
      "bbox": [
        53.99999237060547,
        724.772216796875,
        298.8009948730469,
        733.6787719726562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "enabling discovery of non-trivial contact modes while solv-",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        294.8722229003906,
        558.0009155273438,
        303.7787780761719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ing complicated locomotion and manipulation tasks [22],",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        306.82720947265625,
        558.0009765625,
        315.7337646484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[23]. In the online setting, the optimized policy network can",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        318.7821960449219,
        558.0009155273438,
        327.6887512207031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "be evaluated at real-time rates on onboard computers [14],",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        330.7381896972656,
        558.0010375976562,
        339.6447448730469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[15]. Compared to online MPC, one downside of this offline",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        342.69317626953125,
        558.0009155273438,
        351.5997314453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "policy optimization approach is the significant computation",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        354.6481628417969,
        558.0009765625,
        363.5547180175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and time required to find performant reward functions and",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        366.6031494140625,
        558.0010375976562,
        375.50970458984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hyperparameters for each task.",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        378.5581359863281,
        438.4099426269531,
        387.4646911621094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this paper, we aim to combine the benefits of both",
      "bbox": [
        323.16302490234375,
        390.650146484375,
        558.00146484375,
        399.55670166015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "online MPC and simulation-based RL by solving whole-",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        402.6051330566406,
        558.0010375976562,
        411.5116882324219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "body motion-planning and control problems in real time by",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        414.56011962890625,
        558.0008544921875,
        423.4666748046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "directly sampling over whole-body dynamics and collision",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        426.5151062011719,
        558.0009155273438,
        435.4216613769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "models, without any offline policy optimization.",
      "bbox": [
        313.20001220703125,
        438.4700927734375,
        509.6020812988281,
        447.37664794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
